      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It sounds like you're tapping into a really profound vein of emotional exhaustion, which can be hard to translate onto the page without feeling too personal. To ground Elias, try focusing on the *physical* manifestations of his perpetual drain—the way he holds his shoulders, the specific hesitations in his voice, or the dullness in his movements. Instead of labeling the feeling, show the loop through a mundane, repetitive action he performs each day. This specificity can make the existential weight feel real and unique to his experience.",
      "source": "target",
